-- The interleaved wand (w3-c): the general binding, second spelling: the bind column computed in-program, then the column IS the relation. Twin of 123-modifier-chain.bqn (the interleaved section). (was w3-modifier-chain-c)
-- The same binding computed as a column: a key-valued column has exactly a functional relation's shape, so the value IS the relation. Same wand, same answer, by a different road.
-- scan(min) along revDeck is the .bqn's NextP with the wand row left out — non-projectiles carry their key plus 99, the reverse min-scan finds the next projectile at or after each slot, and the write-back conjugates through the order's grade (Tier 2). A key-valued column has exactly a functional relation's shape, so Bind' resolves to its inverse fibers — the value-level rel — and the damage write is the same grouped fold as w3-b. Same wand, same answer, the relation as value instead of data.
--! registry ../registries/125-modifier-chain-c.reg
--! expect bal = 0 1 3 2 2 1 0
--! expect minBal = 0 1 1 1 1 1 0
--! expect member = 0 1 1 1 1 1 1
--! expect bind = 0 3 3 3 5 5 6
--! expect damage = 0 0 0 13 0 13 3

Spell , Bal = 1 + (+\ (DrawAdd - 1) @ Spell)
Spell , MinBal = 0 - (max\ (0 - Bal) @ Spell)
Spell @ deck & (Slot == 0 | prev.MinBal > 0) , +Member
Spell , Bind = scan(min) (Keys + 99 * (1 - Proj)) along revDeck
Spell & Proj & Member , Damage += 10 * (#/ (Bind' & (Mod & Member)))
